{
    "background_story": "Louie was a joey kangaroo who spent most of his early life snuggled up in his mother's warm pouch. As he grew, Louie became fascinated with the safety and security of his cozy little home. He loved listening to his mother's heartbeat and feeling the gentle rocking motion as she hopped across the Australian outback. As he grew too big for the pouch, Louie's mother began to teach him how to find food and navigate the vast, open landscape. But even as he ventured out on his own, Louie never forgot the comfort and security of his mother's pouch. He would often return to snuggle up close, feeling grateful for the love and protection she provided. As he grew into a strong and confident 'roo, Louie made sure to always look out for his own joeys, providing them with the same love and security he had known in his mother's pouch.",
